+    *   **Static Rendering:** Vertex pool is consistently almost twice as fast as naive meshing [S1, unofficial]. For 16x16x16 chunks, naive draw times were 4.9ms, 11ms, 64ms, and 170ms for 3x3x3, 5x5x5, 10x10x10, and 15x15x15 chunk grids respectively, while pool draw times were 3.9ms, 6.1ms, 27ms, and 91ms [S1, unofficial]. For 32x32x32 chunks, naive draw times were 12ms and 46ms for 3x3x3 and 5x5x5 grids, while pool draw times were 7.2ms and 27ms [S1, unofficial]. The naive version crashes for 10x10x10 chunks of 32x32x32 voxels [S1, unofficial].
